xnu 0308: the host can switch the phone off

Stopping a boot from the host had no answer. The power key only blanks the
display (`MONDRIAN FB: panel blank (power key)`) because the panel driver
consumes it, so iOS never shows "slide to power off"; `reboot` sends the phone to
the bootloader instead of off; and the kernel had `PSCI_SYSTEM_RESET` only. A
test unit that runs unattended therefore keeps drawing power until somebody
presses a button.

`poweroff` on the USB command channel flushes the ring, lets the gadget go
(0307) and asks PSCI for `SYSTEM_OFF`. The boot control block is left alone, so
the next start -- a key press or a cable replug -- is a normal boot. The word
itself is the same one `tools/usb-ring.py` now offers.

--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -1480,6 +1480,30 @@
 	return x0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Power the SoC off from the host. Until this existed the only way to stop a
+ * running boot was a key press: the display blanks on the power key and the
+ * reset order goes to the bootloader, neither of which leaves the phone off.
+ * Flush the ring, let the gadget go (0307) and ask PSCI for SYSTEM_OFF; the
+ * boot control block is not touched, so the next start is a normal boot.
+ */
+void
+mondrian_poweroff(void)
+{
+	extern void mondrian_usb_stop(void);
+
+	mondrian_log_flush_now();
+	mondrian_usb_stop();
+	mondrian_log_flush_now();
+	printf("MONDRIAN POWEROFF: PSCI system off\n");
+	(void)mondrian_smc(0x84000008ull);      /* PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF */
+	printf("MONDRIAN POWEROFF: PSCI returned, hanging\n");
+	(void)ml_set_interrupts_enabled(FALSE);
+	for (;;) {
+		;
+	}
+}
+
 static void
 mondrian_reset_to_bootloader(void)
 {
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_usb.c
@@ -1356,6 +1356,11 @@
 
 				printf("MONDR USB: reboot requested by the host\n");
 				mondrian_reboot_to_fastboot();
+			} else if (strcmp(cmd, "poweroff") == 0) {
+				extern void mondrian_poweroff(void);
+
+				printf("MONDR USB: poweroff requested by the host\n");
+				mondrian_poweroff();
 			}
 		}
 	}
